        "original_id": "f8a6e852-9a9a-5e6f-93a0-9cd84ed50682",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Draiman, Geno Lenardo, Richard Patrick, Brian Liesegang\n- Bands: Device, Disturbed, Filter\n- Places: Cleveland\n- Works: Short Bus, Hey Man Nice Shot\n- Topics: industrial metal, industrial rock\n\nFacts:\n- In 1993, Richard Patrick and Brian Liesegang formed Filter in Cleveland as an American industrial rock group.\n- In 1995, Filter released its debut album, \"Short Bus.\"\n- Filter's 1995 album \"Short Bus\" went platinum and sold over one million copies, largely because of the success of the single \"Hey Man Nice Shot.\"\n- Device was an industrial metal band started by David Draiman, who was the frontman of the heavy metal band Disturbed.\n- Geno Lenardo, the former guitarist of Filter, approached David Draiman, and they began working together on new material that led to Device.",
